                <pb facs="0449" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.116 Fruit/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany (Sackett) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-21T12:00:00+01:00">September 21,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 21—7:48 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. Department’s 111, September 19, 2 p.m. Made informal oral representations
                    yesterday and feel that it was useful to make our views known. Cabinet is again
                    taking up the question tomorrow and will attempt to reach a decision then or if
                    necessary at a further meeting to be held on Saturday. Am reporting by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
